WEBVTT

00:02.280 --> 00:03.480
I'm home!

00:06.040 --> 00:08.520
Huh? And who were you again?

00:09.400 --> 00:10.110
How awful!

00:10.110 --> 00:13.320
Did you really forget your 
mom's face, Kaname-chan?!

00:13.320 --> 00:15.510
Come to think of it, I remember 
there being some mom

00:15.510 --> 00:17.870
who ditched her daughters 
to go hang out overseas.

00:17.870 --> 00:20.080
Your mom was feeling unstable, okay?!

00:20.080 --> 00:23.100
Her husband running off with some 
younger woman was a real shock!

00:23.100 --> 00:25.560
So she tends to do crazy stuff 
out of the blue sometimes!

00:25.560 --> 00:27.120
Do you understand?!

00:27.880 --> 00:30.060
Please say you do!

00:30.060 --> 00:32.890
You actually realize it's crazy, huh?

00:32.890 --> 00:34.480
But it's gonna be okay!

00:34.970 --> 00:39.970
Because your mom has come home with 
a lovely gift for her daughters!

00:40.300 --> 00:42.220
A pair of tickets to a hot spring?

00:42.470 --> 00:46.450
Yep. Seems like my mom won it in a contest.

00:47.480 --> 00:52.580
But we can't go, so I figured I'd 
ask if you and Tsukassan wanted to.

00:53.360 --> 00:55.750
No, no, we couldn't do that.

00:55.750 --> 00:57.750
You should go with your family.

00:57.750 --> 01:00.000
I thought about that,

01:00.000 --> 01:02.750
but they're only good through June.

01:03.040 --> 01:06.480
Which means my sister will 
be in the middle of finals.

01:07.350 --> 01:11.350
I've gotta tend to the bathhouse. 
And as far as mom goes...

01:11.350 --> 01:16.140
Hot springs remind me of my honeymoon 
with my runaway husband.

01:16.140 --> 01:18.790
Why enter the contest, then?

01:19.920 --> 01:20.510
I dunno!

01:20.830 --> 01:23.240
I mean, I'm happy to accept them,

01:23.240 --> 01:24.660
but are you sure?

01:24.660 --> 01:26.340
Of course I'm sure!

01:26.340 --> 01:30.520
Besides, you two haven't actually 
gone on a honeymoon yet, right?

01:31.000 --> 01:32.900
Oh, right...

01:32.900 --> 01:34.380
There you go!

01:37.870 --> 01:41.230
Kaname-chan said to use 
these for our honeymoon.

01:42.440 --> 01:44.580
That's really generous of her.

01:44.580 --> 01:45.490
Right?

01:45.890 --> 01:47.670
What kind of hot spring is it, anyway?

01:47.920 --> 01:49.790
It's supposed to be really amazing.

01:49.790 --> 01:51.920
The rooms come with open-air baths.

01:56.090 --> 01:58.050
Wh-What should we do?

01:59.270 --> 02:00.550
What do you mean?

02:00.980 --> 02:05.060
Well... I mean... it'd be just the two of us.

02:06.750 --> 02:10.040
R-Right... I see what you mean.

02:10.750 --> 02:14.930
But... we're married, so...

02:14.930 --> 02:18.660
We might as well go, right?

02:22.060 --> 02:23.030
Yeah!

03:04.530 --> 03:13.290
TONIKAWA

03:04.530 --> 03:13.290
TONIKAWA

03:54.500 --> 03:59.090
<b>Episode 5      The Exciting Expert of the Hot Springs</b>

03:54.600 --> 03:57.000
All right, you two have fun!

03:57.000 --> 03:59.750
I'll take good care of Toast!

03:59.750 --> 04:03.260
Don't worry about souvenirs! 
Just make sure to enjoy yourselves!

04:04.790 --> 04:07.640
I-It's nice how the weather 
has really cleared up.

04:07.920 --> 04:12.100
G-Good point. Even though it's June.

04:12.100 --> 04:14.260
So... how are we making the trip?

04:14.260 --> 04:16.900
Well... I thought we'd start with the train.

04:17.750 --> 04:20.900
Will we really be able to make 
it there without any trouble?

04:21.870 --> 04:22.780
What do you mean?

04:22.780 --> 04:25.910
Well, remember when we went to Nara before?

04:26.460 --> 04:29.410
Oh, yeah, I remember. 
When Chitose-chan showed up.

04:30.520 --> 04:34.600
Which means we have no idea 
when she might pop up,

04:34.600 --> 04:35.710
so we better be careful!

04:36.240 --> 04:39.960
Wow, a trip to a hot spring? Fancy that.

04:40.180 --> 04:40.770
Huh...

04:40.770 --> 04:42.410
Are we not going after them?

04:42.410 --> 04:43.720
Of course not.

04:43.930 --> 04:48.100
I have stuff to do.
Finals are coming up, and I'm busy!

04:48.340 --> 04:52.640
Besides, I'm not rude enough to crash 
a married couple's private time.

04:52.640 --> 04:57.330
Wow! After all the rude stuff she's 
done before! Chitose is growing!

04:57.330 --> 04:59.070
I'm so proud of you, Chi-chan!

04:59.070 --> 05:02.620
Stop making fun of me!

05:03.610 --> 05:05.610
<b>Hot Spring</b>

05:04.330 --> 05:07.610
Y'know, this might be my first 
time visiting a hot spring.

05:05.610 --> 05:07.610
<b>This train is a special direct service line to the hot spring in Nagano</b>

05:05.610 --> 05:07.610
<b>The time now is:</b>

05:07.610 --> 05:09.560
Have you gone before, Tsukasa-chan?

05:10.100 --> 05:12.070
Oh, good question.

05:12.070 --> 05:15.380
Well, Japanese people have always 
had a fondness for hot springs.

05:15.380 --> 05:17.620
Even Yoshimune liked to visit Kusatsu.

05:18.010 --> 05:22.160
I didn't expect the two of us 
to visit one together, though.

05:22.160 --> 05:24.880
Are you feeling nervous?

05:27.140 --> 05:29.390
Wh-Wh-Wh-Why would I feel nervous?

05:30.390 --> 05:32.890
Well, your face looks a little tight...

05:33.110 --> 05:36.540
I-I-I-I-It's not because
 I'm nervous, not at all!

05:36.540 --> 05:40.150
I'm just looking forward to the hot 
spring so much that I'm shaking!

05:40.150 --> 05:42.550
I see! Well, that's a good thing.

05:42.550 --> 05:46.090
Sure is! W-Would you like to eat lunch?

05:46.090 --> 05:47.280
Oh, sure.

05:47.280 --> 05:51.030
<i>Even if that's true, 
I'm super nervous myself!</i>

05:56.900 --> 05:59.670
Th-This is a huge inn...

05:59.670 --> 06:02.800
I-It really is massive.

06:02.800 --> 06:04.980
Are we sure this is the right place?

06:06.380 --> 06:07.680
It should be...

06:07.680 --> 06:10.300
I guess we should go in for now.

06:14.280 --> 06:17.420
W-Wow!

06:17.420 --> 06:19.610
This is crazy luxurious!

06:20.140 --> 06:22.180
Are you sure this is the right room?!

06:22.180 --> 06:24.820
Yes, it certainly is.

06:24.820 --> 06:30.710
The open-air bath is part of the room, 
but we also have a larger, 24-hour bathhouse,

06:30.710 --> 06:32.830
which you're free to make use of.

06:33.760 --> 06:36.170
I guess this is the right room after all.

06:36.170 --> 06:37.970
L-Looks like it.

06:37.970 --> 06:40.790
Well, since we're here, 
why don't we hop in the bath?

06:41.530 --> 06:44.890
N-No, I meant... the big one!

06:44.890 --> 06:46.590
Oh, of course!

06:49.370 --> 06:54.970
So let's spend an hour in the big bath, 
and then we'll take a look around town.

06:55.280 --> 06:58.270
Right. We'll meet up in the 
room around 4:00 PM, then.

06:58.270 --> 06:59.310
S-Sure.

07:00.560 --> 07:01.350
What is it?

07:02.630 --> 07:05.260
W-Well, it's just...

07:06.330 --> 07:08.360
N-Never mind.

07:09.100 --> 07:11.360
<i>At the moment, I can't help but wonder...</i>

07:11.680 --> 07:14.120
<i>How is Nasa-kun so relaxed?!</i>

07:14.870 --> 07:18.870
<i>I'm completely on edge about 
visiting a hot spring together.</i>

07:18.870 --> 07:22.120
<i>So how is my darling 
maintaining his composure?</i>

07:22.700 --> 07:27.000
<i>Could he be used to it or something?</i>

07:27.280 --> 07:28.730
I'll see you later, then.

07:28.730 --> 07:29.860
Y-Yeah.

07:33.840 --> 07:36.260
Well, I guess I'll hit the bath.

07:45.000 --> 07:47.880
She wasn't kidding when she 
said the baths were big!

07:48.780 --> 07:53.280
Kaname-chan's place isn't bad or anything, 
but you can tell the hot spring difference.

07:53.850 --> 07:57.840
So, here I am, on a hot spring 
trip with Tsukasa-chan...

07:57.840 --> 08:01.290
It doesn't feel real for some reason, 
which would explain why I'm not nervous.

08:02.250 --> 08:08.640
<i>Maybe when a situation is too perfect, you end
 up getting a bizarrely peaceful feeling?</i>

08:08.640 --> 08:11.300
<i>My head's empty. Completely empty.</i>

08:11.300 --> 08:14.550
<i>Almost so quiet that it scares me.</i>

08:15.200 --> 08:17.300
<i>Is this that "water still as 
a mirror" mental state?!</i>

08:17.300 --> 08:22.560
<i>Aw, no! I'm on a hot springs trip with my wife!
 This is no time to reach enlightenment!</i>

08:23.130 --> 08:25.880
It's like a second attempt at a honeymoon!

08:25.880 --> 08:30.470
Which means I need to do everything 
I can to make it a memorable one!

08:31.400 --> 08:33.640
<i>I've got 50 minutes until 
Tsukasa-chan gets out of the bath!</i>

08:33.640 --> 08:36.040
<i>I'll research everything I can 
about Kusatsu in the meantime,</i>

08:36.040 --> 08:38.500
<i>and make sure to provide the best 
escort around town possible!</i>

08:38.500 --> 08:39.950
<i>And with that settled...</i>

08:39.950 --> 08:41.310
Hey, Jiri!

08:41.310 --> 08:43.330
<i>How can I help you?</i>

08:45.080 --> 08:48.340
<i>All right, all right, I think 
I've got the broad outline.</i>

08:48.800 --> 08:52.870
<i>First thing that comes to mind with Kusatsu
 is the Yubatake, with all the hot springs.</i>

08:52.870 --> 08:56.040
<i>Next is yumomi, the water-turning 
process. It's crucial.</i>

08:56.560 --> 08:59.110
<i>There's also getting onsen dumplings,</i>

08:59.110 --> 09:01.360
<i>tempura maitake mushrooms, 
and soba noodles.</i>

09:01.360 --> 09:03.350
<i>And Kusatsu-style mochi 
makes a good souvenir.</i>

09:03.950 --> 09:07.440
<i>If I can cover all these bases, 
this trip will be Kusatsu as heck!</i>

09:07.440 --> 09:10.400
With that settled, 
it's time to get my research on!

09:10.400 --> 09:14.610
I've got 40 minutes left! First, I'll scope 
out the locations on the grounds of the inn!

09:17.360 --> 09:19.640
Sorry, could you help me?

09:19.640 --> 09:22.710
Do you know where the front desk is?

09:23.260 --> 09:26.180
This place is so huge, I'm a bit lost...

09:26.180 --> 09:29.620
Oh... I just got here myself, 
so I'm not really sure.

09:29.620 --> 09:34.230
This place is downright massive. It's hard for
 an old timer to get the lay of the the land.

09:35.370 --> 09:41.310
I wish my husband was here, but he 
passed away so much sooner than me.

09:42.260 --> 09:47.560
Kusatsu meant so much to us, but now that 
I'm here alone, I have no idea what to do.

09:47.560 --> 09:48.360
Then...

09:49.200 --> 09:51.260
In that case, I can show you the way!

09:51.260 --> 09:53.780
Really? Oh, I don't know what to say!

09:54.510 --> 09:57.650
<i>It'll be okay! I still have 30 minutes!</i>

09:57.650 --> 10:01.780
<i>Once I get her to the front desk, 
I'll head straight to the Yubatake!</i>

10:01.780 --> 10:03.790
<b>Ladies</b>

10:23.600 --> 10:26.180
I think young people 
should have more freedom.

10:27.250 --> 10:30.190
Got tired of studying for the finals, huh?

10:30.410 --> 10:34.940
That's right! I'm totally worn out! 
I wanted to go to the hot spring, too!

10:34.940 --> 10:37.600
I wanted to take a bath, get in the sauna, 
drink some milk, and then sleep!

10:37.600 --> 10:39.880
Sleep as much as possible! Do you get me?!

10:39.880 --> 10:42.200
Can't say that I don't, but...

10:42.740 --> 10:45.450
Okay, how about a change of pace, then?

10:45.690 --> 10:47.340
What do you mean?

10:47.340 --> 10:50.390
Well, it might not be a hot spring, 
but this is still a bathhouse,

10:50.390 --> 10:54.840
and once the customers are gone, you can 
use the big baths as much as you want.

10:57.400 --> 11:00.750
That's my Kaname-chan! Thanks!

11:00.750 --> 11:04.100
Aw, it's not that big a deal.

11:09.710 --> 11:10.350
So...

11:11.290 --> 11:13.000
What exactly am I doing?

11:13.000 --> 11:16.320
You're going to be helping 
me out for a change of pace.

11:16.320 --> 11:21.020
What?! So the way I'm changing things 
up is to go from studying to working?

11:21.020 --> 11:22.330
Damn right.

11:22.330 --> 11:26.680
It's not like you're studying to get 
into Tokyo University or anything, right?

11:26.680 --> 11:28.440
You just want to avoid a failing grade

11:28.440 --> 11:30.950
so you don't have to repeat a year. 
That's bare-minimum level.

11:30.950 --> 11:32.870
W-Well...

11:32.870 --> 11:36.780
And if you're so spineless that two or 
three days of that has left you wiped out,

11:36.780 --> 11:41.510
then give up on studying and learn how 
to work right now, you get me?! Slacker!

11:41.510 --> 11:43.890
This is sister abuse...

11:44.220 --> 11:46.360
B-But it's so hard!

11:46.360 --> 11:51.970
I usually sleep through class, so I don't 
understand any of this stuff! Y'know?!

11:51.970 --> 11:55.580
It amazes me how you can be totally honest 
about how you deserve what you're getting.

11:55.580 --> 11:58.500
I've always been good at coming 
up with excuses to slack off!

11:58.500 --> 11:59.650
Yeah, you suck, all right.

12:00.210 --> 12:01.650
But hey, it's all right.

12:03.070 --> 12:07.240
I never thought you'd be able 
to fill in for Tsukassan,

12:07.240 --> 12:08.910
so I called in some help.

12:09.230 --> 12:11.380
"Called in some help"?

12:11.380 --> 12:15.670
Why do I have to help you clean 
up your bathhouse, exactly?!

12:15.920 --> 12:21.170
Why? Well, I figured you'd be lonely with 
Tsukassan away on her hot spring trip.

12:21.440 --> 12:24.760
That doesn't add up to me helping 
with your family business!

12:24.760 --> 12:28.590
And what point is there in wearing 
a swimsuit to clean a bathhouse?!

12:28.590 --> 12:31.760
It's not like I can't 
clean in regular clothes!

12:31.760 --> 12:35.360
But I figured we could have some 
fun since you're in a swimsuit!

12:37.390 --> 12:38.990
What's the big idea?!

12:38.990 --> 12:41.610
Just goofing around for a change of pace!

12:41.610 --> 12:44.650
I never said anything about needing 
a change of pace in the first place!

12:44.650 --> 12:47.950
Don't just stand there, say something!

12:49.020 --> 12:50.030
That's the spirit!

12:50.030 --> 12:53.990
The best part of a bathhouse is seeing 
just how much skin will be on display!

12:53.990 --> 12:57.520
Stop it! You're going to take everything off!

12:57.520 --> 13:01.380
You wanted a change of pace, right?! 
Nudity would be different!

13:01.380 --> 13:03.560
Fine! Two can play at that game!

13:03.560 --> 13:05.380
Stop it!

13:07.810 --> 13:11.370
Ugh, what is the point of 
this cheap sex appeal?!

13:11.370 --> 13:16.060
What even is going on here?! Couldn't we be 
doing something else?! Seriously! Come on!

13:16.060 --> 13:19.310
Oh, yeah! Now it's a real bathhouse episode!

13:19.690 --> 13:21.610
What are you even talking about?!

13:28.110 --> 13:32.770
<i>I have to admit, Yoritomo really hit the 
jackpot when he discovered this place.</i>

13:32.770 --> 13:37.680
<i>There's still something about going on a 
trip together that's embarrassing somehow,</i>

13:37.680 --> 13:39.860
<i>despite living together.</i>

13:40.550 --> 13:42.940
<i>An open-air bath in our room...</i>

13:45.310 --> 13:46.590
N-No more!

13:47.370 --> 13:49.970
I'll overheat if I keep thinking 
about this in a hot bath!

13:50.630 --> 13:53.130
<i>There'll be plenty of time to bathe later,</i>

13:53.130 --> 13:56.600
<i>so I may as well get out a bit 
early and head back to the room.</i>

13:57.350 --> 14:01.360
<b>Reception</b>

13:57.350 --> 14:01.360
<b>Aizawa Hot Springs</b>

13:57.640 --> 14:01.360
You have been such a sweetheart, 
and a huge lifesaver.

14:01.590 --> 14:03.650
Aw, it's nothing.

14:03.650 --> 14:06.070
<i>Just 25 minutes left! 
Gotta get out of here, fast!</i>

14:06.070 --> 14:07.720
W-Well, I should get going...

14:07.720 --> 14:12.400
Oh, no. I don't think I know 
the way back to my room now.

14:12.400 --> 14:16.590
But I can't keep imposing on you...

14:17.600 --> 14:20.020
I-It's okay!

14:20.020 --> 14:22.420
I'll walk you back to your room!

14:23.170 --> 14:25.360
You're sure you don't mind?

14:25.360 --> 14:27.380
O-Of course!

14:27.660 --> 14:33.220
I'm sure your wife must be happy, 
being married to a dear like you.

14:33.810 --> 14:35.490
How'd you know I was married?

14:35.490 --> 14:37.770
It's the ring, honey.

14:38.770 --> 14:44.520
My own husband died early, so I don't have 
as many memories with him as I'd like.

14:46.030 --> 14:48.680
How are you finding married life?

14:48.680 --> 14:50.280
W-Well, let me see...

14:50.950 --> 14:53.030
Every day is full of surprises.

14:53.770 --> 14:57.140
There's so much to enjoy 
and that I don't see coming.

14:59.040 --> 15:02.130
You must really love your wife!

15:02.130 --> 15:03.960
W-Well, that's...

15:04.700 --> 15:07.090
Come, now, no need to be embarrassed.

15:07.660 --> 15:10.590
Being married is truly special.

15:11.040 --> 15:15.810
Nothing like parents, siblings, 
friends, or even lovers.

15:15.810 --> 15:19.110
You'll understand what I mean in time.

15:21.270 --> 15:22.340
Darling?

15:23.180 --> 15:24.530
Oh, Tsukasa-chan.

15:26.720 --> 15:29.740
Hey. What do you think you're doing here?

15:30.770 --> 15:33.900
Tsukasa-chan, do you know this lady?

15:33.900 --> 15:38.070
I more than know her. 
This is Tsukuyomi Tokiko.

15:36.370 --> 15:41.870
Tsukuyomi Tokiko

15:36.370 --> 15:41.870
April 23rd

15:36.370 --> 15:41.870
Age 81

15:38.070 --> 15:41.870
She was our signatory witness 
when we got married.

15:41.870 --> 15:43.410
She's Chitose's grandmother.

15:43.410 --> 15:44.610
What?!

15:44.610 --> 15:45.500
That a problem?

15:46.600 --> 15:49.830
I had no idea! I'm so sorry!

15:49.830 --> 15:52.210
Oh, no, no. It's perfectly fine.

15:52.210 --> 15:55.510
I didn't really mean to trick you, either.

15:55.510 --> 15:58.950
Well, I was actually dead-set on it,

15:58.950 --> 16:01.640
and I'm kind of disappointed 
the ruse is over already.

16:01.640 --> 16:04.020
<i>She's one of those 
honest-but-troublesome types!</i>

16:04.020 --> 16:09.530
This is just mean-spirited! Why would you lie
 just to try and test my good-natured husband?

16:09.530 --> 16:13.320
Now, now, it wasn't a test.

16:13.320 --> 16:16.950
I just used my natural acting 
ability to get close to him,

16:16.950 --> 16:20.180
and then started enjoying myself so much

16:20.180 --> 16:24.610
that I decided to push as far as 
I could to see what would happen.

16:24.610 --> 16:26.940
That's exactly what you call a lie!

16:26.940 --> 16:33.150
You should honestly be praising my 
willingness to push my limits at this age.

16:33.150 --> 16:34.630
Not happening!

16:35.680 --> 16:40.380
I wouldn't have had to come here 
in the first place if you weren't

16:40.380 --> 16:43.230
too embarrassed to introduce your husband.

16:43.230 --> 16:45.440
That doesn't excuse coming 
all the way out here!

16:45.870 --> 16:50.910
Come on, Tsukasa-chan, I should 
still properly introduce myself.

16:52.430 --> 16:56.060
He got you! He got you 
with perfect logic, too.

16:56.060 --> 16:57.620
Quit laughing!

16:58.320 --> 17:01.210
If we're going to do this, 
why don't we head back to my room?

17:01.210 --> 17:05.460
I made sure to get the biggest 
suite on the premises.

17:07.050 --> 17:08.960
Well, let's make this official.

17:08.960 --> 17:13.760
My name is Yuzaki Nasa, 
and I married Tsukasa-san recently.

17:13.760 --> 17:17.600
I know it's a bit late, but I want to 
thank you for acting as our witness.

17:18.050 --> 17:20.100
It's a pleasure to make your acquaintance.

17:22.100 --> 17:25.600
I've been wanting to meet 
you for a long time.

17:25.900 --> 17:27.360
Me?

17:27.360 --> 17:33.450
Of course. I was wondering what kind of 
person could melt the ice queen's heart.

17:33.450 --> 17:34.260
Hey!

17:34.260 --> 17:39.300
I see now, though. Very interesting. 
So this is your type?

17:39.300 --> 17:40.620
You seriously need to stop.

17:40.620 --> 17:44.800
Come on, it's okay. And it's 
honestly a relief to hear.

17:44.800 --> 17:45.870
But still...

17:46.260 --> 17:48.590
Are you really staying in this 
huge room by yourself?

17:48.590 --> 17:52.070
Of course! Despite appearances, I am fairly...

17:52.070 --> 17:53.360
Well, considerably...

17:53.360 --> 17:55.990
Actually, let's say <i>significantly</i> wealthy.

17:55.990 --> 17:57.840
Don't get any ideas, though.

17:57.840 --> 18:02.180
I worked hard to acquire every yen of it in 
the burnt-out rubble at the end of the war.

18:02.680 --> 18:05.880
I was so diligent. A master of diligence.
 Im so impressive!

18:05.880 --> 18:07.850
Am I amazing or what?

18:07.850 --> 18:09.200
She seems fun.

18:09.200 --> 18:10.150
I-I guess...

18:10.570 --> 18:13.370
I can see why she'd choose you, though.

18:13.370 --> 18:16.860
So clever, and so sweet, too.

18:16.860 --> 18:22.410
I was amazed you were able to tell 
that stone was a moon rock so easily.

18:23.140 --> 18:24.550
Moon rock?

18:26.010 --> 18:28.410
Oh, at Chitose-chan's house!

18:29.020 --> 18:32.370
Well, there was the placard 
that listed its makeup.

18:32.370 --> 18:35.050
And you were using nitrogen 
to keep it from oxidizing.

18:35.340 --> 18:38.370
I figured you wouldn't do all 
that if it wasn't the real deal.

18:39.140 --> 18:42.420
I see. Still, it's very impressive, honestly.

18:42.420 --> 18:47.060
Knowing she has a partner like 
you is a great relief for me.

18:47.560 --> 18:52.460
I'm sure you'll be able to 
accomplish what I couldn't...

18:52.460 --> 19:00.570
no, what nobody else has 
been able to all these years.

19:02.080 --> 19:03.450
What do you mean?

19:11.100 --> 19:15.210
<b>Here we go
The Big Three Tour Card</b>

19:11.100 --> 19:15.210
<b>Here we go
The Big Three Tour Card</b>

19:11.570 --> 19:12.280
What's this?

19:12.280 --> 19:15.210
"Here we go! The Big Three Tour Card."

19:15.720 --> 19:17.140
"Here We Go Big Three"?

19:17.140 --> 19:20.880
If you're able to visit the three 
big day-trip hot springs in Kusatsu,

19:20.880 --> 19:25.080
that nice little ticket can earn you the 
title of Kusatsu Hot Springs Expert.

19:25.080 --> 19:26.720
Hot springs expert?!

19:26.960 --> 19:31.440
I get the feeling you'll be up to any challenge

19:31.440 --> 19:33.480
in pursuit of becoming a hot springs expert.

19:33.480 --> 19:35.610
I don't understand where this joke is going.

19:36.740 --> 19:40.610
Enough already! We're not here 
to indulge your comedy act.

19:40.880 --> 19:45.000
You are so mean. And I was 
being completely serious.

19:45.000 --> 19:48.560
Fair enough, though. This should
 be plenty for today.

19:48.560 --> 19:53.460
I'd hate to take up time you could be 
using to fool around here in Kusatsu.

19:53.460 --> 19:55.030
Y-You...

19:55.030 --> 19:56.690
But are you sure about this, Nasa-kun?

19:56.690 --> 19:57.490
What?

19:57.490 --> 20:02.110
I'm sure you've noticed, 
but this girl can be incredibly bashful.

20:02.110 --> 20:07.530
Which means she's awful at expressing 
sentiments like love and affection.

20:09.180 --> 20:12.390
Hey! Darling, don't agree with her!

20:12.920 --> 20:17.610
I'm sure you think you're conveying your 
love without putting it into words,

20:17.610 --> 20:20.180
but you need to be able to say it, too.

20:20.180 --> 20:22.680
Y-You don't need to tell me! I have been!

20:22.680 --> 20:26.190
Whatever you've been doing, I'm pretty 
sure the normal amount would be double,

20:26.190 --> 20:28.410
so you need to work on saying it more.

20:28.410 --> 20:30.410
I don't need your advice!

20:30.940 --> 20:34.560
I say that sort of thing 
when we're alone, so...

20:34.560 --> 20:36.420
I don't need you worrying about it!

20:36.700 --> 20:38.320
Did you hear, that, dearie?

20:38.320 --> 20:42.790
She's going to really express how much 
she loves you once you're alone!

20:42.790 --> 20:44.770
You should get your hopes up!

20:44.770 --> 20:46.430
Uh, yeah...

20:47.030 --> 20:50.180
Could you please shut your mouth?!

20:50.650 --> 20:54.190
I know you usually like to 
march to your own drummer,

20:54.560 --> 20:57.690
but it wouldn't hurt to take a bit 
of advice every now and then.

20:57.690 --> 21:01.170
Well, I hope you two enjoy 
the rest of your trip.

21:01.170 --> 21:04.570
The yumomi process is quite interesting, 
so you should check it out.

21:05.030 --> 21:06.700
Thank you.

21:06.700 --> 21:09.790
Still, I'm truly glad...

21:10.580 --> 21:16.090
that she met someone so wonderful. 
Take good care of her, Nasa-kun.

21:16.090 --> 21:21.340
She can be a pain in certain ways, 
but generally speaking, she's a kind one.

21:21.750 --> 21:22.480
Right!

21:23.330 --> 21:25.340
You never know when to stop, huh?

21:26.740 --> 21:29.350
Honestly, what is her deal?

21:30.730 --> 21:32.720
She's really funny.

21:32.720 --> 21:35.100
And that was some good advice.

21:36.160 --> 21:37.100
What part do you mean?

21:37.630 --> 21:40.110
The stuff about expressing 
your love... maybe.

21:55.370 --> 21:58.830
<b>Closed for the Day</b>

21:55.370 --> 21:58.830
<b>Sorry!</b>

23:25.040 --> 23:40.060
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

23:25.940 --> 23:27.800
What souvenirs should we get for the others?

23:27.800 --> 23:29.940
Kaname wants something 
a little crude and funny,

23:29.940 --> 23:31.930
and Aya mentioned some 
kind of local merchandise

23:31.930 --> 23:33.490
made in collaboration with some anime.

23:33.490 --> 23:35.650
You actually went and asked them! Nice!

23:35.650 --> 23:40.060
Actually, they volunteered the 
info before I could ask them.
